commit bd6681c885feb4edff0c4c9c6ad9e7b5becaf7ff
Author: Qiumiao Zhang <zhangqiumiao1@h-partners.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 3 10:00:00 2026 +0800

    Directly access _type/_name in _to_string to avoid subclass property lock
    
    The previous fix using _unsynchronized_methods list has a limitation:
    SynchronizedMeta.__new__ only checks _unsynchronized_methods from the
    class being defined (dct parameter), not from parent classes. When
    subclasses like LVMLogicalVolumeDevice override 'type' as a @property,
    that override gets wrapped with exclusive() because the subclass doesn't
    inherit the parent's _unsynchronized_methods configuration.
    
    This means the call chain str → _to_string → self.type can still acquire
    blivet_lock on those subclasses, potentially causing deadlock.
    
    Solution: Access _type and _name attributes directly in _to_string()
    instead of going through the property getters. This completely bypasses
    the property mechanism and avoids triggering locks in any subclass,
    regardless of whether they override type/name properties.
    
    The trade-off is that LVM devices with mixin-based type overrides would
    show their base _type (e.g. "lvmlv" instead of "lvmthinpool") in __str__
    output, but that seems fine for logging/debugging.
    
    Suggested-by: Tony Asleson <tony.asleson@gmail.com>
    Signed-off-by: Qiumiao Zhang <zhangqiumiao1@h-partners.com>

