commit 1504da5ebeabf966c5cea354e14345ec5b26a6ae
Author: Vojtech Trefny <vtrefny@redhat.com>
Date:   Tue Jun 9 13:43:39 2026 +0200

    Fix original_format not set on MD arrays due to sysfs race
    
    When the MDRaidMember populator helper creates an MD array, it calls
    handle_device(update_orig_fmt=True) to detect and record the array's
    format as original_format. However, this call is gated on
    md_array.status which reads md/array_state from sysfs. Due to a race
    condition, the array state may not yet be active, causing the call to
    be skipped entirely.
    
    When the main scan loop later processes the array device, it calls
    handle_device without update_orig_fmt, so original_format is never
    updated from its initial empty DeviceFormat(None).
    
    This causes failures during device destruction: the LUKS format
    teardown (which calls cryptsetup close) relies on original_format
    to close the dm-crypt mapping before mdadm --stop runs. With
    original_format stuck at None, the LUKS device is never closed,
    and mdadm --stop fails with "Cannot get exclusive access".
    
    Update the condition in handle_device to also set original_format
    when it was never properly initialized (type is None) and a real
    existing format has been detected by handle_format.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

