    devicetree: match btrfs subvol mount options with or without a leading slash
    
    The subvol= fstab mount option names a path relative to the top-level
    subvolume (see btrfs(5)). Existing systems may use subvol=/@ while blockdev
    reports the subvolume as @. Strip the leading slash from the fstab value
    when comparing to the device name, as MountsCache does for mountinfo paths.
    
    https: //btrfs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/btrfs-man5.html#mount-options
    Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

