commit f2086c4d22d6ef125947526c2fc56fc85fcd97ae
Author: Vojtech Trefny <vtrefny@redhat.com>
Date:   Wed May 27 14:33:46 2026 +0200

    Read data and metadata RAID levels for existing btrfs volumes
    
    Read RAID levels from sysfs /sys/fs/btrfs/<uuid>/allocation/{data,metadata}/
    during subvolume listing, when the volume is known to be mounted. The kernel
    exposes the RAID profile as a subdirectory (e.g. single, dup, raid1).
    raid1c3 and raid1c4 are normalized to raid1.
    
    Discovery bypasses btrfs-specific creation validators and uses
    raid.ALL_LEVELS directly, so levels like raid5/raid6 that are not
    offered for new volumes are still correctly recorded on existing ones.
    
    Resolves: #1175
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

