Date:   Tue Mar 10 12:22:16 2026 +0100

    tasks: Fix FAT filesystem min size calculation always returning zero
    
    The expression subtracted free_cluster_count from itself instead of
    from cluster_count, always producing zero. This meant the minimum
    size was always reported as 32 MiB regardless of actual data on disk,
    which could lead to data loss when shrinking a FAT filesystem.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit f040fd67354b49967f00c7e2b96c29ca8c3e6185
Author: Vojtech Trefny <vtrefny@redhat.com>
Date:   Tue Mar 10 12:19:38 2026 +0100

    threads: Fix inverted guard condition in save_thread_exception
    
    The condition checked "is None" instead of "is not None", causing
    the function to always return early without saving anything. Since
    both globals start as None and only this function sets them, the
    thread exception propagation mechanism was completely non-functional.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

